# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Secrets & environment — API keys live in environment variables, never in the repo
.env
.env.*
*.key
secrets.json

# Runtime data generated by the agent.
#
# scan_log.jsonl and processed_files.json are deliberately NOT ignored. The
# scheduled GitHub Actions scan runs on a throwaway machine that is deleted
# minutes later, so if its findings were not committed back they would simply
# vanish and every run would re-review the same documents forever. Committing
# them is what makes the repo itself the agent's memory. They hold only the
# agent's own verdicts on the sample contracts in inbox/, which are ours.
#
# approvals.json stays ignored: those are a named human's approve/reject
# decisions, and a compliance officer's sign-offs are not public-repo material.
approvals.json

# Documents uploaded through the dashboard — someone else's contracts, which
# have no business in a public repo
uploads/

# Live-status heartbeat written by monitor.py while it runs. Pure ephemeral
# runtime state (is the watcher alive right now) — not part of the repo, and
# unlike scan_log.jsonl / processed_files.json it is NOT the agent's memory.
heartbeat.json

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Backup copies of the runtime files, made by hand while testing. The real
# scan_log.jsonl and processed_files.json ARE committed (see above); their
# .bak twins are local scratch and have no business in a clone.
*.bak

# Streamlit
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Claude Code local/personal settings (not part of the project)
.claude/settings.local.json
